bin
# Dockerfile.test is a `COPY . .` build. Both of these exist on a normal working
# copy - gitignored, not absent - and hold database dumps, pgBackRest WAL
# archives, and the compose secrets readme.md tells operators to create.
backups
.env.compose

**/.terraform
**/*.tfstate
**/*.tfstate.*
**/terraform.tfvars

*.log
*.tmp
*.swp
.DS_Store
coverage*

# The console is built in its own stage from web/package-lock.json. Both of
# these exist on a normal working copy and neither may reach the Go build:
# node_modules is a several-hundred-megabyte host artifact, and a host-built
# bundle would be embedded in place of the one the image just built.
web/node_modules
internal/dashboard/webassets/bundle/dist
